account`."},"fingerprint":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/DigestMultibase","description":"Present with `sealed`: a digest identifying the stored credential, so an administrator can tell which one is set without anyone being able to read it. Computed over the credential with a community-held key, never a bare hash of a low-entropy secret."},"setAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"Present with `sealed`: when the stored credential was last set."},"roomsHoldingCredentials":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"Present with `vta-account`: how many rooms the community currently holds a live room-scoped credential for."}}},"ExternalAccountId":{"title":"ExternalAccountId","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"pattern":"^[a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9-]{0,62}[a-z0-9])?\$","description":"The identifier of an external account held by the community\'s VTA (the external/accounts/* family), which issues the community short-lived, room-scoped credentials and holds the long-lived authority itself."},"DigestMultibase":{"title":"DigestMultibase","description":"A cryptographic digest as a multibase-encoded multihash — the encoding the W3C Verifiable Credentials Data Model 2.0 defines for `digestMultibase`, and the one `did:webvh` uses for its SCID and entry hashes.\\n\\nMultihash carries the hash algorithm in-band, so the value is self-describing and the wire format survives an algorithm change without a schema revision; multibase does the same for the base encoding, so a verifier never infers base58 from base64url by context. A bare hex string or a `sha-256:`-style prefix hard-codes one algorithm into the wire contract and is non-conforming here.\\n\\nThis definition constrains the *encoding only*. What the digest is computed over is stated by each referencing field, because it differs legitimately: a digest over a JSON document is taken over its RFC 8785 (JCS) canonicalization, while a digest over an opaque artifact is taken over its bytes. A field whose input is a JSON document and which does not name a canonicalization is not reproducible.\\n\\nRestricted to the two multibase headers W3C Controlled Identifiers 1.0 §2.4 normatively requires — `z` (base58btc) and `u` (base64url-no-pad). CID permits others but states that \\"interoperability is not guaranteed between implementations using such values\\", and a registry whose purpose is interoperability should not mint digests a conforming verifier may be unable to read. The alphabets are enforced rather than assumed: base58btc excludes 0, O, I and l, and an earlier permissive pattern let three published examples carry digests that were not valid base58 at all. base58btc is RECOMMENDED, for consistency with `did:key` and `did:webvh`.","type":"string","minLength":16,"pattern":"^(z[1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]+|u[A-Za-z0-9_-]+)\$","examples":["zQmbWqxBEKC3P8tqsKc98xmWNzrzDtRLMiMPL8wBuTGsMnR"]},"StorageConfig":{"title":"StorageConfig","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["id","label","settings","state","createdBy","createdAt"],"description":"One storage config as the community holds it. Carries no secret.","properties":{"id":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/StorageConfigId"},"label":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128,"description":"A display name for administrators (`EU — S3 (main account)`). Shown to a room\'s creator with the config\'s kind when the community lets them choose."},"settings":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/StorageSettings"},"auth":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/StorageAuth"},"capacityBytes":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"Total ciphertext bytes the community will store on this config, across every room assigned to it. A capacity, not a policy: an upload that would cross it is refused with scope `storage`. Absent means no capacity set."},"state":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/ConfigState"},"isDefault":{"type":"boolean","description":"True for the config a room is assigned to when neither the community\'s policy nor its creator names one."},"createdBy":{"type":"string","pattern":"^did:","maxLength":2048},"createdAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"updatedBy":{"type":"string","pattern":"^did:","maxLength":2048},"updatedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}}},"ConfigState":{"title":"ConfigState","type":"string","enum":["active","draining","retired"],"description":"`active`: accepts new rooms and new uploads. `draining`: retired by an administrator while blobs still name it — refuses new rooms and new uploads, keeps serving reads, and becomes `retired` when a migration has emptied it. `retired`: refuses new rooms and new uploads and holds no blob. A config is never deleted while a blob names it."},"StorageAuth":{"title":"StorageAuth","description":"How the community authenticates to a config\'s backend. Absent on a `local` config, which needs none.\\n\\n`vta-account` (RECOMMENDED): an external account in the community\'s VTA. The VTA holds the long-lived authority; the community holds nothing that outlives a credential lifetime, and asks for credentials scoped to one room\'s prefix for at most 15 minutes, every issuance audited at the VTA. Required for a `walrus` config other than a `sealed` one, since the VTA\'s `sui-signer` account signs its storage transactions.\\n\\n`ambient`: the cloud identity of the machine the community runs on (an instance role, workload identity), downscoped to one room\'s prefix by the community itself. Not audited or rate-limited by the VTA, and usable by anything on that machine that reaches the metadata endpoint. Not valid for `walrus`.\\n\\n`sealed` (discouraged): a long-lived credential stored by the community, set with vtc/storage/credentials/set. Protects against every administrator through every surface the community offers; does not protect against whoever operates the machine.","oneOf":[{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["mode","account"],"properties":{"mode":{"const":"vta-account"},"account":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/ExternalAccountId"}}},{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["mode"],"properties":{"mode":{"const":"ambient"}}},{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["mode"],"properties":{"mode":{"const":"sealed"}}}]},"StorageSettings":{"title":"StorageSettings","description":"A config\'s backend settings, discriminated by `kind`. Never a secret: a credential is a StorageAuth, held elsewhere.","oneOf":[{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/LocalSettings"},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/S3Settings"},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/GcsSettings"},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/WalrusSettings"}]},"WalrusSettings":{"title":"WalrusSettings","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["kind","relayUrl","aggregatorUrl","epochs","extendBeforeEpochs"],"properties":{"kind":{"const":"walrus"},"relayUrl":{"type":"string","format":"uri","maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^https://","description":"The Walrus upload relay the community writes through. The community never runs a publisher: a publisher holds a hot wallet in its own configuration, which is the long-lived secret these tasks exist to avoid."},"aggregatorUrl":{"type":"string","format":"uri","maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^https://","description":"The Walrus aggregator the community reads through."},"epochs":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":53,"description":"Storage epochs to buy when a blob is registered. Walrus sells storage in epochs (two weeks on mainnet) and caps one purchase at 53."},"extendBeforeEpochs":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":52,"description":"How many epochs before a live blob\'s end epoch the community extends it. A blob that has become an orphan is not extended, and lapses: the Walrus form of deletion."}}},"GcsSettings":{"title":"GcsSettings","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["kind","bucket"],"properties":{"kind":{"const":"gcs"},"bucket":{"type":"string","minLength":3,"maxLength":222,"pattern":"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{1,220}[a-z0-9]\$","description":"The bucket name. Validated against GCS naming rules here, because it is placed in a Credential Access Boundary condition and must never carry anything but a name."},"prefix":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/ObjectPrefix"}}},"ObjectPrefix":{"title":"ObjectPrefix","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":256,"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9!_.*\'()/-]+/\$","description":"A key prefix inside the bucket, ending in `/`, under which the config\'s `rooms/` tree is placed. Restricted to the S3 safe-character set so that it can be placed in a downscoped policy without escaping."},"S3Settings":{"title":"S3Settings","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["kind","region","bucket"],"properties":{"kind":{"const":"s3"},"endpoint":{"type":"string","format":"uri","maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^https://","description":"The S3 API endpoint, for a store other than AWS (R2, B2, MinIO). Absent means AWS S3 in `region`. HTTPS only."},"region":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"pattern":"^[a-z0-9-]+\$","description":"The bucket\'s region, as the store names it (`eu-west-1`; `auto` for R2)."},"bucket":{"type":"string","minLength":3,"maxLength":63,"pattern":"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9.-]{1,61}[a-z0-9]\$","description":"The bucket name. Validated against S3 naming rules here, because it is placed in downscoped session policies and must never carry anything but a name."},"prefix":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/ObjectPrefix"},"pathStyle":{"type":"boolean","description":"Address the bucket in the path rather than the host name, as MinIO usually needs. Absent means virtual-hosted style."}}},"LocalSettings":{"title":"LocalSettings","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["kind","root"],"properties":{"kind":{"const":"local"},"root":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1024,"pattern":"^/","description":"Absolute path of the directory the community writes blobs under, on its own host. Created owner-only. Not carried by the community\'s backup: back it up beside it."}}},"StorageConfigId":{"title":"StorageConfigId","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"pattern":"^[a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9-]{0,62}[a-z0-9])?\$","description":"A storage config\'s identifier, chosen by the administrator who creates it and immutable thereafter: lowercase letters, digits and inner hyphens, at most 64 characters (`eu-s3-primary`, `walrus-main`). Unique within the community. Never reused after a config is retired, because blobs name their config by this value."}}}';

